 "aerobic": true,
 "description": "Modified M9 minimal medium with casamino acids (wet-lab, for growth assays informing iEC1073) — a minimal medium extracted from Carter et al. (2024). Mapped to BiGG from the paper's stated composition.",
 "namespace": "bigg",
 "provenance": {
  "source_type": "literature",
  "citation": "Carter et al. A temperature-induced metabolic shift in the emerging human pathogen Photorhabdus asymbiotica. mSystems (2024). DOI: 10.1128/msystems.00970-23. [PMC11575385]",
  "doi": "10.1128/msystems.00970-23",
  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11575385/",
  "notes": "Extracted from the primary paper (snippet: using a modified M9 salt buffer at pH 6.8 (12.5 mM Na2HPO4, 8.5 mM NaCl, 22 mM KH2PO4, 2 mM MgSO4, and 100 µM CaCl2), 20 mM glucose, 0.05% (wt/vol) casamino acids and a trace element solution modified). Component names mapped to BiGG (see mapping_confidence); presence-based bounds unless the paper gave exchange bounds; concentration_mM where units allowed. Extraction confidence: high.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "base_expansion": "Base 'M9' expanded to standard composition: M9 minimal medium (Sambrook & Russell 2001): Na2HPO4, KH2PO4, NaCl, NH4Cl, MgSO4, CaCl2 + carbon source.",
  "verification_evidence": "using a modified M9 salt buffer at pH 6.8 (12.5 mM Na2HPO4, 8.5 mM NaCl, 22 mM KH2PO4, 2 mM MgSO4, and 100 µM CaCl2), 20 mM glucose, 0.05% (wt/vol) casamino acids and a trace element solution modified from Helmholtz Zentrum München (13.4 mM EDTA, 3.1 mM FeCl3·6H2O, 0.62 mM ZnCl2, 8.1 µM MnCl2·4H2O, 76 µM CuCl2·2H2O and 42 µM CoCl2·2H2O). Growth was measured at 28°C.",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
